  "description": {
    "text": "Melee! Pokémon Scramble × Pokémon Card Game (乱戦！ポケモンスクランブル×ポケモンカードゲーム), a boxed board game released in Japan on 10 July 2009, after the WiiWare video game Melee! Pokémon Scramble came out on 16 June. Players set their cards on a board drawn like the game's arena and take turns trying to knock each other's Pokémon out. The box held the board, 16 battle cards, 14 player markers, 52 damage counters, four Energy dice and a guide, and the cards could also be used in official tournaments.\n\nThree more cards, Pachirisu, Croagunk and Eevee, numbered past the set's 16 and marked with the Pokémon Daisuki Club logo, went to the winners of a lottery the fan club ran for players of the video game that summer: only 100 copies of each exist. The English edition, Pokémon TCG: Rumble, followed in December 2009 with the 16 cards.",
    "sources": [
      {
        "title": "PocketMonsters.net: 'Melee! Pokemon Scramble x Pokemon Card Game' Announced (16 June 2009)",
        "url": "https://pocketmonsters.net/news/548"
      },
      {
        "title": "WikiDex: Pokémon Rumble (TCG)",
        "url": "https://www.wikidex.net/wiki/Pok%C3%A9mon_Rumble_(TCG)"
      },
      {
        "title": "Elite Fourum: Rumble Pokemon x Pokemon Daisuki Club Secret Rare Cards",
        "url": "https://www.elitefourum.com/t/rumble-pokemon-x-pokemon-daisuki-club-secret-rare-cards/22749"
      },
      {
        "title": "ICv2: Preview of 'Pokemon Trading Card Game: Rumble' (13 November 2009)",
        "url": "https://icv2.com/print/article/16268"
      }
    ]
  },
  "tell": {
    "text": "A \"乱\" mark at the bottom right, and a number out of 016",
    "sources": [
      {
        "title": "PocketMonsters.net: 'Melee! Pokemon Scramble x Pokemon Card Game' Announced (16 June 2009)",
        "url": "https://pocketmonsters.net/news/548"
      }
    ]
  },
